  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The なければ form",
     "texto": [
      "To say «I have to», take the verb in the **ない** form, drop the **い** and add **なければ**: **おき** + **なければ** → **おきなければ** (I have to get up).",
      "With **する** it becomes **しなければ**, and with **くる** it becomes **こなければ**. For group 1 verbs the ない form changes the last letter to **あ** (のむ → のまない → のまなければ)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Two ways of saying it",
     "texto": [
      "**〜なければ なりません** and **〜なければ いけません** mean the same: **はやく おきなければ なりません** (I have to get up early).",
      "They are polite forms. In casual speech **〜なきゃ** is said."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
